From b9c6a2bdc4102e716f614f951cb9415f89fa658a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anaskassar786 <Anaskassar786@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 16:39:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deploy): replace dead OpenRouter models, restore TLS
 verification, silence SSL warning

Three production issues reported from the deployed environment.

1. Every configured OpenRouter model was unavailable, so all AI features fell
   back. Verified every candidate live against
   https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models/{id}/endpoints on 2026-08-28: the entire
   2025 :free generation is gone (llama-3.1-8b-instruct, llama-3.3-70b-instruct,
   qwen3-coder, deepseek-chat-v3-0324, gpt-oss-20b, glm-4.5-air,
   nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b all return an empty endpoint list and
   nemotron-3-nano-omni is a hard 404). Replaced them with slugs that resolve to
   a live endpoint on four different providers, so one provider outage can no
   longer silence the whole fallback chain. AI_MODEL_FALLBACK2 and
   AI_COMMAND_MODEL_FALLBACK both pointed at the dead nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b.

2. NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 disables certificate verification for every
   outbound HTTPS call in the process. No code set it, so the fix is two-sided:
   delete it from the deployment environment, and add enforceSecureTls() so a
   leftover value cannot survive a deploy. Node re-reads the variable at connect
   time, so restoring it at startup is effective (proved against a live
   self-signed TLS handshake).

3. The pg-connection-string SSL warning is silenced at the source by rewriting
   sslmode=prefer|require|verify-ca to verify-full in databaseConfigFromEnv.
   Those modes are aliases today but stop verifying the server certificate in
   pg v9, so this also removes a silent security downgrade on that upgrade.
   uselibpqcompat is respected as an explicit opt-out.

Verified: pnpm build, pnpm typecheck and pnpm test (256 files / 3320 tests) all
pass, plus 16 new tests for normalizePostgresSslMode and enforceSecureTls.
